OL,3,AAction on knife crime needed more than
OL,4,Aever, says Damilola Taylor's brother
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe brother of schoolboy Damilola
OL,7,FTaylor, killed in an attack in Peckham
OL,8,F26 years ago, has said work to tackle
OL,9,Fknife crime is "needed now more than
OL,10,Fever".
OL,12,FThe 10-year-old was fatally stabbed
OL,13,Fwhile on his way home from Peckham
OL,14,FLibrary in south London on 27 November
OL,15,F2000.
OL,17,FBabatunde (Tunde) Taylor now chairs the
OL,18,FDamilola Taylor Trust, set up by their
OL,19,Fparents in his brother's memory. It
OL,20,Fworks to provide support for
OL,21,Fdisadvantaged children vulnerable to
OL,22,Ffalling into crime.
OL,23,APub: 11-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,311,300,200,140,0,100
